INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,url_slug,status,updated_at,created_at) VALUES
('recursion','Recursion','minion','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"recursion","name":"Recursion","team":"minion","ability":"Each night, choose up to █ players (different to last night) & information: it replaces their ability''s info until dusk if possible. [█ is known before setup]","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Recursive Room (SCP-970) is the room which leads to the Recursive Room which leads to the Recursive Room which leads to the Recursive Room which leads to the Recursive Room which leads to the Recursive Room which leads to the Recursive Room...","summaryBullets":["The Recursion''s chosen targets gets information from their ability overwritten, even if they are drunk or poisoned.","The Recursion does not affect information gained by other means, such as when the Storyteller explains the rules, a player''s character or alignment changes, or when another player''s ability is giving the information to the Recursion''s target.","Additionally, the Recursion cannot override information with that which is impossible for the character to reasonably receive, whether its because it''s the invalid type, or a certain output isn''t possible for the current context of the character or game."],"howToRun":["While setting up the game, before deciding on what character tokens to put in the bag, publicly announce what the Recursion''s █ variable will be for this game. You may choose to make it a standard unchanging number, or a number that varies based on conditions being met {{i|(Ex. \"2 (on odd-numbered nights) or 3 (on even-numbered) nights\", or \"1 or 3 (if a Minion was executed today).\")}}. Regardless of your choice, write down the number {{i|(and any of it''s conditions it may have)}} on a piece of paper or on a phone.","Each night, wake the Recursion. They point at up to █ players, nods yes, then signals either finger signals, characters on the script, other players, head nods, thumbs up or down, and any other type of ability target, or a combination of any. Mark the Recursion''s chosen targets with the **BLINDED** reminder, and write the information provided on a piece of paper, or on a phone. Put the Recursion to sleep.","While a player is marked with the **BLINDED** reminder and they are sober & healthy, you must give the respective information the Recursion provided whenever their ability prompts you if that information is applicable and possible for their ability. Whilst this does override an ability initially misregistering a target and getting false information as a result of it {{i|(such as Recluse or Spy)}}, it **does not override the drunkenness and poisoning states'' arbitrary information.**","Each dusk, the blinded players are no longer affected - remove their **BLINDED** reminder."],"examples":["During the night, the Recursion selects the Chambermaid and the Mathematician with the information \"4\". The Chambermaid wakes to select 2 players that woke tonight and learns a 2, whilst the Mathematician learns 4 players affected when the real number was 3.","During the night, the Recursion selects the Fortune Teller and Artist with the information \"yes\". The Fortune Teller selects the Demon and learns \"yes\", and the upcoming day, the Artist asks a question with a negative answer, and learns \"yes\"."],"quote":"The end is never the end is never the end is never the end is never the end is never the end is never the end is never the end is never...","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Fisherman","align":"good","text":"If the Recursion chooses the Fisherman with various pieces of information, their ability will yield advice that implicates some facts using that information.","id":"fisherman"},{"name":"Savant","align":"good","text":"If the Recursion chooses the Savant with a ''yes'', or a ''no'', their ability instead yields 2 pieces of true information, or false information respectively.","id":"savant"},{"name":"Prognosticator","align":"good","text":"The Recursion cannot affect the Prognosticator''s Prophecy.","slug":"prognosticator"},{"name":"Astronomer","align":"good","text":"If the Recursion chooses the Astronomer with various pieces of information, their ability will yield a reason that implicates some facts using that information.","id":"astronomer_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Beachcomber","align":"good","text":"The Recursion will learn what off-script Townsfolk ability the Beachcomber will learn with tommorow, and can affect the Beachcomber as they would that character.","id":"beachcomber_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Bug Collector","align":"good","text":"The Recursion cannot affect the Bug Collector''s picture.","id":"bugcollector_circus_music"},{"name":"Historiographer","align":"good","text":"If the Recursion chooses the Historiographer with various pieces of information, their ability will yield a reason that implicates some facts using that information.","id":"historiographer_temporary_box"},{"name":"Longxing","align":"good","text":"The Recursion cannot affect the Long Xing''s Dark Fate.","id":"longxing_temporary_box"},{"name":"Musician","align":"good","text":"If the Recursion chooses the Musician with a number between negative 4 to positive 4, their ability will yield a response indicating the level of intensity towards \"fully there\" (or \"progress undone\" for negative).","id":"musician_temporary_box"},{"name":"Charlatan","align":"evil","text":"The Charlatan''s information disruption overrides the Recursion''s.","id":"charlatan_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Plotter","align":"good","text":"If the Recursion chooses the Plotter with various pieces of information, their ability will yield advice that implicates some facts using that information.","id":"plotter_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Unicorn","align":"good","text":"The Recursion cannot affect the Unicorn''s unlikely tale.","id":"unicorn_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Visitor","align":"good","text":"The Visitor''s information disruption overrides the Recursion''s.","id":"visitor_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Sibyl","align":"evil","text":"The Recursion cannot affect the Sibyl''s Profecy.","id":"sibyl_darkartists_stuff"}],"firstNight":12.97,"otherNight":23.97,"reminders":["Blinded","Blinded","Blinded","?"],"setup":true,"firstNightReminder":"The Recursion points to up to █ (which is publicly revealed before the tokens are finalized and put into the bag) players, shows the ''yes'' head signal, then signals either finger signals, characters on the script, other players, head nods, thumbs up or down, and any other type of ability target, or a combination of any. The information yielded by their abilities is replaced with yours where its applicable to the information they''d normally get from their ability.","otherNightReminder":"The Recursion points to up to █ (which is publicly revealed before the tokens are finalized and put into the bag) players, shows the ''yes'' head signal, then signals either finger signals, characters on the script, other players, head nods, thumbs up or down, and any other type of ability target, or a combination of any. The information yielded by their abilities is replaced with yours where its applicable to the information they''d normally get from their ability.","art":"art/recursion.png","jsonId":"recursion_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/recursion','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('wallbehind','Wallbehind','minion','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"wallbehind","name":"Wallbehind","team":"minion","ability":"Each night, a good player gets a riddle. If today''s answer wasn''t correct & a living evil is executed, they only register as dead.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Wallbehind is living street art that hides not in the walls, but on the walls.","summaryBullets":["The Wallbehind is able to submerge an evil player into the walls should a designated good player fail to overcome it''s attraction.","Any good player can learn today''s riddle, including the living, dead, repeat targets, or new targets each time.","The riddle the player gets should be about anything regarding the gamestate if it is reasonably answerable.","The good player who gets the question then has to answer it by the end of today, or any executed evil player will not actually die, but appear to be.","They can only answer it once that day, either publicly, or privately.","Evil players already feigning death cannot be protected by this ability again.","There is no feedback for answering a riddle right or wrong.","If the Wallbehind then dies whilst any evil player is registering as dead, those evil players do not suddenly die, and do not appear to be resurrected."],"howToRun":["Before each riddle you will give out, remember to write it on a piece of paper or on a phone.","Each night, wake any good player. Show them their riddle, move the **BLINDSIGHTED** reminder by their character token, and put them to sleep.","Once per day, when the good player marked with **BLINDSIGHTED** answers the riddle, either verbally, via text, publicly, or privately, register it. If it is correct, remove their **BLINDSIGHTED** reminder token.","If a living evil player {{i|(those registering as dead don''t count to this)}} is executed but **BLINDSIGHTED** reminder token still remains, they remain alive. Declare that they died, but do not add a shroud to that evil player {{i|(flip the life token on the Town Square, as normal.)}} From now on, that evil player registers as dead."],"tips":["Typically, the same repeat good player gets the riddle each time for as long as the Wallbehind has their ability. As the evil team is winning though, feel free to also assign the day''s riddle to another good player as to confirm them, and the currently active existance of the Wallbehind."],"quote":"Who?","iconBy":"le_nuberto","customBoxes":[{"title":"Credit","content":"Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto. Help: @_varii"},{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run","content":"For if the concept of feigning death is too much for your players to handle, use this JSON to replace it with basic protection against death by execution.\n\nBefore each riddle you will give out, remember to write it on a piece of paper or on a phone.\n\nEach night, wake any good player. Show them their riddle, move the BLINDSIGHTED reminder by their character token, and put them to sleep.\n\nOnce per day, when the good player marked with BLINDSIGHTED answers the riddle, either verbally, via text, publicly, or privately, register it. If it is correct, remove their BLINDSIGHTED reminder token.\n\nIf an evil player is executed but BLINDSIGHTED reminder token still remains, they remain alive. Declare that they live, but not explain why.\n\n**Wallbehind █-** (Minion)\nEach night, a good player gets a riddle. If today''s answer wasn''t correct & an evil is executed, they don''t die.\n\n**First night:** Show a good player their riddle.\n**Other nights:** Show a good player their riddle.\n**Reminders:** Blindsighted\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto. Help: @_varii"}],"firstNight":71.1155,"otherNight":92.1155,"reminders":["Blindsighted"],"setup":false,"firstNightReminder":"Show a good player their riddle.","otherNightReminder":"Show a good player their riddle.","art":"art/wallbehind.png","jsonId":"wallbehind_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/wallbehind','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('prosecutor-scp-fragmented-veil','Prosecutor','minion','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"prosecutor-scp-fragmented-veil","name":"Prosecutor","team":"minion","ability":"Thrice per game, choose a player & guess their character: If correct, they die, even if some reason, they could not.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-2578 is a supernatural collective that punishes those who use their character and status to push for an authoritative fascist standard.","summaryBullets":["Thrice per game at night except the first, the Prosecutor chooses a player and guesses their character by pointing to its icon on the character sheet. If the guess is correct, they die, even if they are protected from death in any way, such as from an ability. If the guess is incorrect, nothing happens.","The Prosecutor''s ability is affected by drunkenness and poisoning, as normal."],"howToRun":["Each night except the first, wake the Prosecutor. They either shake their head no or point at any player, then point at any character icon on their character sheet. Put the Prosecutor to sleep.","If the chosen player is the character from the chosen character icon, that player {{i|dies}} - mark them with the **DEAD** reminder. This cannot be prevented in any way {{i|(except if the Prosecutor doesn’t have their ability, such as if they’re drunk or poisoned.)}} Regardless of if the target was killed or not by a correct guess, **the Prosecutor loses an ability charge** - mark them with either the **2 USE** reminder, the **1 USE** reminder if they already have that reminder, or the **NO ABILITY** reminder if they already have that reminder and remove their night token from the night sheet."],"quote":"SIC SEMPER TYRANNIS. I never miss my mark. Abdicate and you will live.","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Plague Doctor","align":"good","text":"If the Plague Doctor dies, a living Minion gains the Prosecutor''s ability in addition to their own ability, and learns this.","id":"plaguedoctor"},{"name":"Spy","align":"evil","text":"The 1st time the Spy sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.","id":"spy"},{"name":"Widow","align":"evil","text":"Once the Widow sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.","id":"widow"},{"name":"▼","align":"evil","text":"The 1st time the Spy sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.","slug":"scp-1936"},{"name":"Esper","align":"evil","text":"The 1st time the Esper sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.","id":"esper_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Bloodless","align":"evil","text":"Once the Bloodless sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.","id":"bloodless_darkartists_stuff"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"Credit","content":"Ability: @legitch, Town of Salem 2. Image: @le_nuberto"},{"title":"Alternative JSON","content":"For if you want the Prosecutor to not be able to end the game abruptly with their ability, use this JSON.\n\nThis Prosecutor cannot kill on the final night, which is typically when only 4 or 3 players are left alive, or an evil win-condition is fast approaching. When this occurs, mark them with the NO ABILITY reminder token.\n\n**Prosecutor █-** (Minion)\nThrice per game, choose a player & guess their character: If correct, they die, even if some reason, they could not. On the final night, you lose this ability.\n\n**Other nights:** If the Prosecutor has not yet fully used their ability: the Prosecutor either shows the ''no'' head signal, or points to a player, and a character on their sheet. If correct, that player dies.\n**Reminders:** 2 use, 1 use, No ability, Dead\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch, Town of Salem 2. Image: @le_nuberto\n\n**Jinxes:**\nPlague Doctor: If the Plague Doctor dies, a living Minion gains the Prosecutor''s ability in addition to their own ability, and learns this.\nSpy: The 1st time the Spy sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.\nWidow: Once the Widow sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.\n▼: The 1st time the Spy sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.\nEsper: The 1st time the Esper sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.\nTiresias: The 1st time the Seer sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights.\nBloodless: Once the Bloodless sees the Grimoire, the Prosecutor cannot kill for 2 nights."}],"firstNight":0,"otherNight":53.2578,"reminders":["2 use","1 use","No ability","Dead"],"setup":false,"otherNightReminder":"If the Prosecutor has not yet fully used their ability: the Prosecutor either shows the ''no'' head signal, or points to a player, and a character on their sheet. If correct, that player dies.","art":"art/prosecutor-scp-fragmented-veil.png","jsonId":"prosecutor_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/prosecutor','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));
